### Exercise 6 — HCQL: CQL over HTTP
#
# Run these with the VS Code REST Client extension (humao.rest-client, already recommended
# for this project): click "Send Request" above any request below. No shell needed — works
# the same on Windows, macOS, and Linux.
#
# HCQL = CQL over HTTP: POST a plain-text CQL statement, get {"data":[…]} back.
# `cds watch` must be running with @odata @hcql enabled on TravelService (Exercise 6).
# Load the sample travels and bookings first; the expand query selects travels with bookings.

@host = http://localhost:4004
@auth = alice:

### A simple CQL query as a plain-text POST body
POST {{host}}/hcql/travel
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}
Content-Type: text/plain

SELECT from Travels { ID, description, totalPrice, currency.code as currency } limit 3

### A deep read with an expand — verbose in OData, one natural query here
POST {{host}}/hcql/travel
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}
Content-Type: text/plain

SELECT from Travels { ID, description, bookings { pos, flightPrice, currency.code as currency } } where exists bookings limit 2

### A filtered, ordered query
POST {{host}}/hcql/travel
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}
Content-Type: text/plain

SELECT from Travels { ID, description, beginDate } where status.code = 'O' order by beginDate desc limit 5
